#: ../../source/docs/common-openpilot-revo-mini.rst:96
#: 91e7ae749fe84189a82e909d97f07659
msgid ""
"First time flashing ArduPilot requires to boot your device in DFU mode to "
"flash an ArduPilot compatible bootloader and firmware file."
msgstr "首次刷写 ArduPilot 需要将设备启动到 DFU 模式，以刷写 ArduPilot 兼容的引导程序和固件文件。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-openpilot-revo-mini.rst:99
#: 183a4c588a114463af18bb7879965df3
msgid "Enter DFU Mode"
msgstr "进入 DFU 模式"

#: ../../source/docs/common-openpilot-revo-mini.rst:100
#: 9b0f7cb9628842ccb4c2dd5a3344bf17
msgid ""
"To do this, you'll need to locate and short two pads on the device. On "
"fullsize Revolution they are designated as \"SB\" or \"SBL\":"
msgstr "为此，您需要找到并短接设备上的两个焊盘。在全尺寸 Revolution 上，它们标记为「SB」或「SBL」："

#: ../../source/docs/common-openpilot-revo-mini.rst:105
#: 32f9299a5747466aa18d7feaee882bce
msgid "On RevoMini they are located here:"
msgstr "在 RevoMini 上，它们位于此处："

#: ../../source/docs/common-openpilot-revo-mini.rst:110
#: 3f444c01e52f47aeabdcdc0e94dec37e
msgid ""
"You can short the pads in any particular way (either with a wire, solder "
"joint, or something else). Detailed instructions are available on the `Revo "
"Mini LibrePilot Wiki "
"<https://librepilot.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LPDOC/pages/29622291/Recover+board+using+DFU>`__."
" A small wire is the easiest way to short the device. You can also power the"
" device via USB first, and then short the pads if using a wire. Once you "
"have the device in DFU mode and connected to your machine continue with the "
"following steps to :ref:`load ArduPilot firmware onto ChibiOS boards "
"<common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards>`."
msgstr ""
"您可以用任何方式短接焊盘（导线、焊接或其他方法）。详细说明可在 `Revo Mini LibrePilot Wiki "
"<https://librepilot.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LPDOC/pages/29622291/Recover+board+using+DFU>`__"
" 找到。使用细导线是短接设备最简单的方式。您也可以先通过 USB 给设备供电，然后再用导线短接焊盘。将设备置于 DFU "
"模式并连接到计算机后，继续按以下步骤操作：:ref:`将 ArduPilot 固件加载到 ChibiOS 板子 <common-loading-"
"firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards>`。"

